  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe machine check compared every tool's catalog rpm with the mounted machine's spindle window. A touch probe's token rpm (1 for the catalog `PRB-0400`) therefore refused **every probing program on a machine that states a spindle minimum**, the Tormach 770MX's 175 rpm among them, with \"tool … runs 1 rpm, below the machine's 175\". The post never commands that number: it forces rpm 0 for a probe, and since #523 starts no spindle for one.\n\n`posting::posted_rpm(tool)` is now the one answer to \"what speed does the program command\": 0 for a probe, the tool's own rpm for every cutter. The post and the spindle-range clause of `machine::check_document` both read it, so they can never disagree again. Every cutter is still judged by its own rpm.\n\nFound while building the contributor's hands-on probe files for #521 on a real 770MX; the test project needed an rpm workaround that this PR makes unnecessary.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `probe_spindle_range`, 3/3:\n  - `a_probe_program_passes_the_spindle_range_of_a_tormach`: a Probe op with the catalog probe raises no rpm problem against the shipped Tormach 770MX. With the fix reverted it fails with the exact refusal above.\n  - `a_probe_posts_no_speed_and_a_cutter_its_own`\n  - `a_cutter_below_the_minimum_is_still_refused_beside_a_probe`: a 100 rpm end mill beside the probe is still refused, and only it.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` (app suites, 451 s): green. Named: `machine` 32, `machine_library` 11, `posting` 17, `probe_op` 11, `conformance` 6. No golden changed; clippy `-D warnings` clean.\n- Fork synced at v0.15.0.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA probing program posted on a real 770MX. That is #521's hands-on test, which currently carries the rpm workaround.\n\nChangelog: A probing program is no longer refused by the machine check for its probe's rpm; only speeds a program commands are judged against the spindle range (#565)\n\nFixes #565\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
